   201	In fact (3.2) is saturated: every branch meets a smooth point of the
   202	exceptional divisor transversely once, `ell_i=1` on the support of `a`, and
   203	`M'.H'=0` locally.  A branch through an exceptional node or tangent to the
   204	exceptional divisor would already contribute more than one and violate
   205	(3.3).
   206	
   207	There is a second exact filter.  Put `Z=sum h_iE_i`.  Crepancy and
   208	orthogonality of the Cartier pullback give
   209	
   210	```text
   211	K_Xtilde.E_i=0,
   212	H'.Z=-Z^2,
   213	p_a(H)-p_a(H')=-Z^2/2=h^t C h/2=h^t a/2.              (3.4)
   214	```
   215	
   216	The curves `H` and `H'` have the same normalization, irreducible-component
   217	count, and normalization genera.  Applying the normalization genus formula
   218	locally to (3.4) yields
   219	
   220	```text
   221	delta_p0(H)
   222	  = h^t a/2 + sum_(q over p0) delta_q(H')
   223	  >= h^t a/2.                                         (3.5)
   224	```
   225	
   226	Together with (2.2),
   227	
   228	```text
   229	h^t a<=8.                                              (3.6)
   230	```
   231	
   232	If equality holds, the minimal surface resolution already separates and
   233	smooths all three strict boundary germs.  If `h^t a=6`, exactly one unit of
   234	curve delta remains upstairs and is removed only by the later embedded
   235	boundary resolution.
   236	
   237	## 4. Exhaustive connected local list
   238	
   239	Use the promoted connected-type theorem and its standard numbering:
   240	
   241	```text
   242	A_r: 1--2--...--r;
   243	D_r: 1--2--...--(r-2), with spin vertices r-1,r at r-2.
   244	```
   245	
   246	Apply `sum a=3`, the exact `A/D` Cartier congruences, positivity of
   247	`h=C^{-1}a`, and `h^t a<=8`.  The resulting list, modulo diagram
   248	automorphisms, is:
   249	
