   252	| `A_r`, `2<=r<=8` | `2e_1+e_(r-1)` and its reversal | `6` |
   253	| `A_r`, `4<=r<=8` | `e_1+e_2+e_(r-2)` and its reversal | `8` |
   254	| `D_4` | `e_1+e_3+e_4` | `6` |
   255	| `D_5` | `e_1+2e_4` (spin reversal equivalent) | `8` |
   256	| `D_6` | `e_1+e_5+e_6` | `8` |
   257	
   258	For `r=2`, the first A-row means `3e_1` and its reversal.  For `r=4`,
   259	the second means `e_1+2e_2` and its reversal.  The two global `A_3`
   260	embedding tags (balanced `B_4` and unbalanced `U_3`) have the same local
   261	Cartier row but remain distinct carrier geometries.
   262	
   263	For completeness, the A-list follows at once from
   264	
   265	```text
   266	sum_i i*a_i=0 mod (r+1),
   267	(C_A^-1)_(ij)=min(i,j)*(r+1-max(i,j))/(r+1).
   268	```
   269	
   270	Distributing three units gives the displayed quadratic values six and
   271	eight; every remaining integral distribution has value at least ten.  For
   272	`D_r`, the two exact congruences
   273	
   274	```text
   275	a_(r-1)=a_r mod 2,
   276	2*sum_(i<=r-2)i*a_i+(r-2)a_(r-1)+r*a_r=0 mod 4
   277	```
   278	
   279	and the promoted inverse formulas give precisely the three displayed rows;
