xmodel/max12-912-order3-nu-q8-infinity-primitivity-review-claude-20260825.md:43:**Decisive evidence.** `Z!=0` is not implicit: infinity report section 2 derives `r8` nonconstant from `9*r8'=j/u`, `j!=0`, `u!=0`, hence `S=r8^9` and `Z=S/nu^10` nonzero and nonconstant — exactly the terminal review's section 10 discharge route (i). Unit inventory, each traced to a reviewed parent: `pi0=nu/n0` nonzero (gate `n0` unit, fibre `nu!=0`); `S0=rho0^9` and `S1` units (leaf4 claim 3 gcd certificates over `E`, valid at all eight contacts by `gcd(Q8,Q8')=1`); `Z0=S0/nu^10!=0`; `lambda^3=Z0` so `lambda!=0` and finite (balanced degrees, terminal review section 7); `3*lambda^2!=0` in characteristic zero. Orders: `ord_infinity(pi∘phi)=0` since `pi(q_Q8)=pi0` is a nonzero finite value, so `ord_infinity(theta)=2a` with `a=ord_infinity(a0)`, `a0 in C(x)` (Kummer-fixed). Positivity: `theta(q_Q8)=0` and `phi(infinity)=q_Q8` give `2a>0`; finiteness: `a0 ≡ 0` would force the quotient image into the `w=0` locus, which meets `C_Q8` in finitely many points, contradicting surjectivity. The formal expansion `S-S0=S1*theta+O(theta^2)` pulls back functorially along the completed local map at `infinity`, `S1` is a nonzero constant, and the tail has order `>=4a`, so `ord_infinity(Z-Z0)=2a`, which is (4.2). Cubing: `Z-Z0=(T-lambda)(T^2+lambda*T+lambda^2)` and the cofactor takes the value `3*lambda^2!=0` at `infinity`, so `e_pass=ord_infinity(T-lambda)=2a`, even and `>=2` — the parity of `e_pass` traces to the parity-involution square `theta=a0^2/pi`, not to the Kummer cube; the report keeps `e_pass` and the Kummer order three explicitly distinct. Decisive cross-check: (4.5) gives `deg(h)=3*(e_pass+1)=3*(2a+1)`, which coincides exactly with the normalization-jet review section 7 independently derived necessary condition `deg(h)=3*(2e+1)` with `e=a`. Two independent routes agree.
xmodel/max12-912-order3-nu-q8-infinity-primitivity-review-claude-20260825.md:51:**Decisive evidence.** `ord_infinity(T-lambda)=deg(B_T)-deg(A_T-lambda*B_T)` for balanced degrees, so `deg(C_T)=D-e_pass` exactly — this is the terminal review's reviewed `e=D-deg(G)`. Coprimality: `gcd(A_T,B_T)=1` (reduced), and any common factor of `C_T` with either divides the other since `lambda!=0`. Squarefreeness of `C_T`: identical to the reviewed "every finite lambda-preimage is simple" (terminal review section 8, point 1); the infinity report's re-derivation via the Wronskian-support condition (3.3) is the same argument (a multiple root `x0` of `C_T` has `B_T(x0)!=0`, hence `A_T(x0)!=0`, yet `W(x0)=0`, contradicting `support_finite(W) ⊂ supp(A_T*B_T)`). Radical count: pairwise coprimality gives `deg rad = r+s+(D-e_pass)`, and the reviewed `r+s=e_pass+1` yields `D+1`, valid also at the edge `e_pass=D` (`C_T` a nonzero constant, contributing zero). Mason–Stothers for the coprime, not-all-constant identity `A_T+(-lambda*B_T)=C_T` bounds `max-deg=D <= (D+1)-1=D`: equality. The polynomial Mason statement carries no separate infinity term; the infinity ramification `e_pass-1` over `lambda` is exactly what the reviewed Riemann–Hurwitz saturation `r+s=e_pass+1` encodes, which is why equality holds. Decision, as charged: Mason sharpness is only a non-obstruction — the bound is met, no passport is excluded, and the reviewed `D=1,2` cyclic controls plus the section 6 control witness nonempty survivors. No promotion beyond a classification signal is made.
