xmodel/sol-approaches.log:5898:Bucket rows and columns by a 0–35 character ID after symbolic preprocessing, reduce the blocks independently, then merge pivots in global monomial order. The reported $278\text{k}\times753\text{k}$ matrix would have average blocks near $7.7\text{k}\times20.9\text{k}$, although a histogram must be measured because balance is not guaranteed. **CONJECTURE (performance):** memory drops close to the number of occupied balanced blocks and arithmetic improves superlinearly; implementation requires an msolve/Groebner.jl backend change.
