xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3228:notes.md:289:- 2026-08-07 night 5 (905db83): A3L1 review — ALL FRONTS CONFIRMED, both promoted. CANONICAL BOOK: td<=5 CLOSED (0 survivors, independent of AF2); td=6 = 4 single-pole r9/M2 (thesis-forced entries) + two-pole residue A on the unique rigid template (merged child (6,12,3,2,5)@0, a1/a2=2+sqrt3). Endgame agents launched: (1) lam_root>=1 ledger attack (cuts 8->4), (2) coefficient-level template lift (genome -> edge consistency -> formal candidate or death edge; sizes farm computation if candidate). Errata E1-E9, five proof-level.
xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3803:SIGRAY-AUDIT.md:84:Of the 72 items audited (thesis pp. 7–30, Not 2.1 → Prop 6.2): **21 VERIFIED, 33 VERIFIED_WITH_NIT, 9 ERRATUM, 2 KNOWN_ERRATUM, 7 GAP**. Cross-check against the campaign catalogue (SHEET6-CAMPAIGN.md §7 = E1–E4 + G1–G3; E5 in SHEET6-III.md; E6–E7 in SHEET6-AF2.md; E8–E9 in SHEET6-AF3.md; E10–E11 in SHEET6-LT-REVIEW.md §6): E1–E7, E9, E11 and G1–G3 all concern §9/assembly (pp. 42–60) and do not touch this batch; the only catalogued items in scope are **E8** (Prop 5.1's cosmetic "Proposition 8" cite-slip — reconfirmed as filed) and **E10** (St 3.15 label swap — independently reconfirmed with exact witnesses; its casualty Prop 5.2 matches LT-REVIEW's FILING FIX 1 exactly). Accordingly, the two KNOWN_ERRATUM verdicts (St 3.15, Prop 5.2) are the catalogue's E10 items, while **all 9 ERRATUM verdicts are NEW**: St 3.7 (missing κπ(F) ∈ N hypothesis in (5)), St 3.8 (D ∈ Z falsified by Not 3.5's P-presentation — this upgrades the campaign's standing H5a convention to printed-statement-forced), St 3.11 (missing prime in (ii) + false equality-propagation clause), St 3.12 (duplicated identity, no (0,x) clause), St 3.13 (false for a ≠ 0; Not 3.13's p_{f−a} slip; recommended E12-candidate), St 3.18 (ε dropped from the unique-continuation conclusion), Prop 5.3 (ratio inverted in (ii)/(viii)), Prop 5.5 (proof-level g-subscript drops + "Statement 18" dangler), and Prop 6.2 (hypothesis F/G swap, same family as E10). Of the 7 GAP verdicts, one is the campaign's known-but-unnumbered **H5a** (Not 3.5 ambiguity, SHEET6-III.md §5 / SHEET6-HIII-REVIEW.md Front 4); the other six are NEW: St 3.14 (cross-fiber Ω alignment/conjugation twist in (ii)), Prop 4.2 (l_j ≠ 0 inference fails at constant-leading-part vertices; the "(7) automatic" Remark is circular), Prop 5.1 (b = 0 argument breaks at g(P) ∈ C* punctures — beyond the catalogued cosmetic E8), Prop 5.4 (q-half of the η^ν-structure never proved; verified repair supplied), Prop 5.8 (no proof printed; the "for ANY a" strength needs an unwritten a-uniformity argument), and St 6.2 (the "in particular" clause needs an H ∈ T_a⁺ hypothesis). A recurring uncatalogued slip family — Not 3.13's p_F/d_F must read p_{f−a,F}/d_{f−a,F} — drives the St 3.13 erratum and riders on Not 3.14, St 3.14, St 3.15 (hypothesis), and St 3.16; the campaign already computes with the corrected reading throughout. Three filing fixes are owed independently of new numbering: SHEET6-H3.md §2a (St 3.12) and SHEET6-A2P-REVIEW.md (St 3.18) present silently corrected text as "verbatim" quotes, and SHEET6-A3L1-REVIEW.md quotes Prop 5.3(ii)'s inverted ratio unflagged.
xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3806:SIGRAY-AUDIT.md:93:- **Prop 5.4 [GAP]** — its (i)/(ii) η^ν-patterns are the source of St 5.2(ii)'s ν-menu, used verbatim by TDUNIFORM (R2) (PROMOTED prime theorem) and AF3's parity pin (PROMOTED, A3L1-REVIEW confirmed). The q-half those results consume is exactly the unproven half; the verified repair in this audit (using α ≥ 2) should be banked as the supporting derivation.
