xmodel/sol-rooftop.log:3488:Two hard conclusions are now clear. First, Hodge/Teissier log-concavity has exactly the wrong direction: it proves nonnegativity of the energy, not an upper bound. Second, normalized multi-Rees finite generation proves only per-pair finiteness; I found a fixed-type family with the same balanced leading power and energy \(B^2-B/\beta\), so no \(B\)-independent constant can come from finite generation, convexity, or leading-form alignment alone. The remaining usable input is the full constant-Jacobian boundary identity.
