xmodel/as-b8-max12-affine-w3-kuranishi-solved-review-grok-20260825.md:93:RREF of the constant `276 x 172` matrix `A3` has rank 104 and 68 free columns. Dual-AWS `result.json` records `w2_rank=104`, `w2_kernel_dimension=68`, and `T0==parent_sol2`. The particular vector has support only in the `R`-block at monomials `x^2 y` and `x y^5` with coefficients `1` and `2`, which is the already-confirmed digit `R2=x^2 y + 2 x y^5`, `S2=0`.
xmodel/as-b8-max12-affine-w3-kuranishi-solved-review-grok-20260825.md:106:with `L(T)=jac(P0,S)+jac(R,Q0)`, `J(T)=jac(R,S)`, and `cross(T,W)=jac(R,B)+jac(A,S)`. On the `W2` fibre, `L(T) ≡ u^2 (mod 3)` and `det(F0)-1=-3u^2`, so `det(F0+3T)-1` is divisible by 9 and the `W3` obstruction is `L(W) ≡ -(det(F0+3T)-1)/9 (mod 3)`. Solvability is the vanishing of the left-cokernel projection `pi` of that residual. The left kernel of `A3` has dimension `276-104=172`, matching `ambient_cokernel_dimension`.
xmodel/as-b8-max12-affine-w3-kuranishi-solved-review-grok-20260825.md:187:The fresh operator is the same matrix `A3` at every predecessor. Rank 104 and kernel dimension 68 are therefore constant, not sampled. Compatibility `kappa(t)=0` is precisely residual-in-image, so a particular `W` exists exactly on the predecessor scheme. RREF of a constant matrix is a linear function of the right-hand side; the residual is polynomial in `t`; the particular solution is therefore a global polynomial section. The total space is the graph of that section plus a constant 68-plane, i.e. a trivial affine `A^68`-bundle over reduced `A^27`, hence `A^95`. No nilpotent thickening: `(s22,s26)` is prime.
xmodel/max12-812-order24-coefficient-infinity-review-grok-20260825.md:357:Every nonzero `(p,c,r)` appears exactly once. In lowest terms, `n=2` forces `m` odd, `n=3` forces `gcd(m,3)=1`, and `n=4` forces `m` odd. The numerator `m` is unbounded. Extra vanishing of some `B_i` (e.g. `B_4=p^2+2r=0` with `p,r\neq 0`, or `B_0=r^2` of weight `8`) only adds `B`-constraints or is redundant with `n\mid 4`; it does not create a new stratum of `(p,c,r)` and does not enlarge the possible `n` beyond four.
